## 🏆 Learning Objectives Checklist

<div style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,#00c9ff,#92fe9d);padding:2em;border-radius:2em;box-shadow:0 2px 16px #00c9ff44;">
  <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Track your progress through the array concepts:</h3>
  <ul style="font-size:1.2em;">
    <li><b>Foundational Level</b></li>
    <ul>
      <li>[ ] I can declare and initialize arrays</li>
      <li>[ ] I understand array indexing</li>
      <li>[ ] I can access and update array elements</li>
    </ul>
    <li><b>Application Level</b></li>
    <ul>
      <li>[ ] I can use loops to traverse arrays</li>
      <li>[ ] I can perform insert, delete, and update operations</li>
      <li>[ ] I can write simple algorithms using arrays</li>
    </ul>
    <li><b>Analysis Level</b></li>
    <ul>
      <li>[ ] I can trace through array logic in existing code</li>
      <li>[ ] I can identify array logic errors in programs</li>
      <li>[ ] I can explain how arrays manage data efficiently</li>
    </ul>
    <li><b>Mastery Level</b></li>
    <ul>
      <li>[ ] I can design array-based solutions for new problems</li>
      <li>[ ] I can implement advanced array algorithms (sorting, searching)</li>
      <li>[ ] I can optimize array usage for clarity and efficiency</li>
    </ul>
  </ul>
</div>

